      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Summary",
      "pageStart": 4,
      "pageEnd": 4,
      "target": "../sections/sec-000-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Thiomersal poses a theoretical low risk of neurodevelopmental toxic-\nity in infants. The known risk of morbidity and mortality from vaccine-\npreventable diseases and of contaminated multidose vaccine vials far\noutweigh any potential risk posed by thiomersal. However, with the\nweight of public opinion against the use of mercury of any sort, WHO\nand other agencies have begun the process of reducing and removing\nthiomersal from vaccines. In the short term (the next 3 years), modifi-\ncations to existing strategies will result in a reduction in exposure to\nthiomersal. Over the long term (beyond 3 y",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "An English summary stating that thiomersal carries a theoretical low risk to infants, far outweighed by the risks of vaccine-preventable disease and contaminated vials, and outlining short- and long-term plans to reduce it in vaccines.",
